📐 Conversion Formulas
Celsius → Fahrenheit
Fahrenheit = (Celsius × 9/5) + 32
Fahrenheit → Celsius
Celsius = (Fahrenheit - 32) × 5/9

⚙️ How It Works

The program follows these steps:
1.Asks the user to enter a temperature value.
2.The user can enter q to quit.
3.Asks whether the temperature is in Celsius or Fahrenheit.
4.Checks the selected unit.
5.Applies the appropriate conversion formula.
6.Rounds the result to 2 decimal places.
7.Displays the converted temperature.
8.If the user enters something other than C or F, a friendly error message is displayed.
9.The program repeats until the user enters q.

💻 Example Run
Celsius to Fahrenheit
Enter temperature value or (to quit press q): 100
Is this in Celsius or Fahrenheit? (C/F): C

====================================

100.0°C = 212.0°F

====================================

Fahrenheit to Celsius
Enter temperature value or (to quit press q): 98.6
Is this in Celsius or Fahrenheit? (C/F): F

====================================

98.6°F = 37.0°C

====================================


Invalid Unit
Enter temperature value or (to quit press q): 100
Is this in Celsius or Fahrenheit? (C/F): X

====================================

Invalid input. You can choose C or F

====================================


Quit
Enter temperature value or (to quit press q): q

====================================

Bye

