🔢 Rounding the Result
The program uses round() to display the converted temperature with a maximum of 2 decimal places.

For example:

round(f, 2)
and:
round(c, 2)

This makes the output easier to read.


🔄 Continuous Conversion
The program uses:
while True:
|->This allows the user to convert multiple temperatures without restarting the program.


The loop stops when the user enters:

q

The program then uses:

break

to exit the loop.


